BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//Littoralicious//Terroir Diani//EN
X-WR-CALNAME:Diani — eat & drink checklist
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-1@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Madafu — The green drinking coconut\, machete-opened on the sand\; hand it back after and ask for the kuna — the shell-slice spoon.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mah-DAH-foo. The coast's original soft drink\, from the tree over 80% of coastal farm households live off\; KES 50–100 settled beach rate (obs. 2026). Best: Any vendor with a panga\; Kongo Beach by the mosque is the classic
LOCATION:Any vendor with a panga\; Kongo Beach by the mosque is the classic
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Kongo+Mosque+Diani+Beach
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-2@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mnazi — Coconut palm wine\, tapped morning and evening from the cut flower spathe — sweet and fizzing fresh\, sour by dusk\; the ferment never stops.
DESCRIPTION:Say: m-NAH-zee. The Digo drink and a documented 2\,800-tapper economy\; legal\, licensed\, and still poured in unsigned village mangwe. Best: Guided only — the Kaaribu tour's mangwe stop\, or the Kaya Kinondo village tasting
LOCATION:Guided only — the Kaaribu tour's mangwe stop\, or the Kaya Kinondo village tasting
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Tsunami+Garden+Cafe+Ukunda
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-3@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Samaki wa kupaka — Whole reef fish char-grilled\, then smeared in spiced coconut cream and finished over the coals.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sah-MAH-kee wah koo-PAH-kah. Kupaka means 'to smear' — the smoke under the coconut is the signature the tourist copies skip. Best: Ukunda's Swahili kitchens\; Coast Dishes when open
LOCATION:Ukunda's Swahili kitchens\; Coast Dishes when open
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Coast+Dishes+Diani
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-4@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pweza wa nazi — Octopus simmered in coconut milk — the reef's toughest catch made silk.
DESCRIPTION:Say: PWEH-zah wah NAH-zee. A Diani–Chale fishery staple that rarely reaches tourist menus\; Karafuu's pweza soup is KES 300 (obs. 2026-08). Best: Karafuu\, Ukunda town\; or off the boats at Mwaepe
LOCATION:Karafuu\, Ukunda town\; or off the boats at Mwaepe
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Karafuu+Restaurant+Ukunda
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-5@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mahamri na mbaazi — Cardamom-coconut doughnut triangles fried in coconut oil\, dipped in pigeon peas stewed in coconut milk.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mah-HAHM-ree nah m-BAH-zee. Mandazi becomes mahamri only when coconut milk enters the dough — the coast's own morning triangle\, gone by 08:00. Best: Ukunda's dawn mama stalls\; Coast Dishes for the seated version
LOCATION:Ukunda's dawn mama stalls\; Coast Dishes for the seated version
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ukunda+town+Kenya
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-6@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Pilau ya pwani — Rice browned in stock with cumin\, cardamom and cloves — the coast's celebration pot.
DESCRIPTION:Say: pee-LAU yah PWAH-nee. The word sailed here: English 'pilau' traces through Turkish to Persian pulaw\, on the same monsoon that built this coast. Best: Swahili Pot or Moiz in Ukunda\; Fridays are the best bet
LOCATION:Swahili Pot or Moiz in Ukunda\; Fridays are the best bet
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Swahili+Pot+Ukunda
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-7@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Coast biryani — The layered\, wetter Swahili-coast cousin — rice with the mchuzi poured over.
DESCRIPTION:Say: bir-YAH-nee. Biryani and pilau share one Persian lineage\; the coast argues the difference daily at lunch. Best: Moiz Swahili Dishes\, Ukunda — early\, while it is fresh
LOCATION:Moiz Swahili Dishes\, Ukunda — early\, while it is fresh
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Moiz+Swahili+Dishes+Ukunda
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-8@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Viazi karai — Boiled potatoes in turmeric gram-flour batter\, deep-fried in the karai\, doused in chilli-tamarind ukwaju.
DESCRIPTION:Say: vee-AH-zee kah-RYE. The Kenyan coast's defining street snack — and the junction's grills do it better and cheaper than any hotel menu. Best: Ukunda junction vendors from late afternoon
LOCATION:Ukunda junction vendors from late afternoon
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ukunda+junction+Diani
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-9@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mishkaki — Charcoal skewers of beef or goat\, garlic-ginger-lime marinade — an evening food by convention.
DESCRIPTION:Say: mish-KAH-kee. The Swahili coast's after-dark protein\, eaten standing where the coals are. Best: Ukunda junction after sunset
LOCATION:Ukunda junction after sunset
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ukunda+town+Kenya
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-10@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Whole grilled reef fish — Changu or snapper off the morning ngalawa\, judged by eye and gill\, grilled over charcoal at the landing.
DESCRIPTION:Say: sah-MAH-kee. The shortest supply chain on the strip: boat to coals in metres\, at prices no beach-road room can match. Best: Colobus Shade or the fishermen's own table at Mwaepe landing
LOCATION:Colobus Shade or the fishermen's own table at Mwaepe landing
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Mwaepe+fish+landing+Diani
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-11@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:The Wasini crab lunch — Grilled crab bought daily off the dugouts\, eaten under a palm roof over the channel — the dhow day's table since 1978.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KAH-ah — crab. Charlie Claw's has fed the Kisite crossing for nearly fifty years\; the crossing is the point\, the crab is the reward. Best: Charlie Claw's\, Wasini Island — as part of the full dhow day
LOCATION:Charlie Claw's\, Wasini Island — as part of the full dhow day
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Wasini+Island+Restaurant
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-12@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kuku choma — Charcoal-grilled chicken with kachumbari — the town benchmark order.
DESCRIPTION:Say: KOO-koo CHO-mah. Ukunda's grills price it for residents: KES 355 at Karafuu (obs. 2026-08). Best: Karafuu\, Ukunda town\, evening off the grill
LOCATION:Karafuu\, Ukunda town\, evening off the grill
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Karafuu+Restaurant+Ukunda
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-13@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mchicha wa nazi — Greens simmered in coconut milk — the side that explains the whole kitchen.
DESCRIPTION:Say: m-CHEE-chah wah NAH-zee. KES 120 at a town grill\; the coconut ladder reaching the vegetable plate. Best: Karafuu or any Swahili canteen in Ukunda
LOCATION:Karafuu or any Swahili canteen in Ukunda
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ukunda+town+Kenya
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-14@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Mango\, Ngowe — The coast's slender\, fibreless classic mango — in season roughly November to January.
DESCRIPTION:Say: n-GO-weh. Kwale's own orchards flood the stalls in season\; the best cheap thing on the strip. Best: Roadside fruit tables and the Mvindeni market\, Dec–Jan
LOCATION:Roadside fruit tables and the Mvindeni market\, Dec–Jan
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Diani+Modern+Market+Ukunda
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-15@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kilifi oysters — Kenyan-coast rock oysters\, farmed up the coast at Kilifi.
DESCRIPTION:Say: oysters. The proof Kenya has an oyster: KES 1\,300 the starter in the cave (obs. 2026-08). Best: Ali Barbour's Cave\; Sails when the coast supplies
LOCATION:Ali Barbour's Cave\; Sails when the coast supplies
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ali+Barbour%27s+Cave+Restaurant+Diani
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-16@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Sugarcane juice — Pressed to order at Ukunda town stands — ask for lime and ginger.
DESCRIPTION:Say: muah — sugarcane. The town's working refreshment\, pressed while you watch. Best: Ukunda town stands\, mornings
LOCATION:Ukunda town stands\, mornings
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Ukunda+town+Kenya
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-17@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Smoked Negroni — The house twist at the coast's only 50 Best Discovery bar.
DESCRIPTION:Say: neh-GRO-nee. Three straight years a Spirited Awards MEA Top-10 honoree — in a Diani courtyard. Best: Funky Monkey\, Wednesdays for salsa night
LOCATION:Funky Monkey\, Wednesdays for salsa night
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Funky+Monkey+Diani
END:VTODO
BEGIN:VTODO
UID:diani-liste-18@littoralicious.com
SUMMARY:Kentaste coconut cream — The take-home: coconut cream pressed minutes from the beach\, 30\,000 nuts a day from 4\,000 Kwale smallholders.
DESCRIPTION:Say: ken-TAST-eh. The local\, traceable pantry coconut — on the shelf at Carrefour and Chandarana. Best: Carrefour Diani or Chandarana\, by the case
LOCATION:Carrefour Diani or Chandarana\, by the case
URL:https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Carrefour+Diani+Centre+Point
END:VTODO
END:VCALENDAR
